  "caption": "Quinn missed the car badly. The logic: \"I can walk, so I can drive.\" Then, in the parked car, doubts arrived.\n\nKay explains that returning to driving is about being able to brake hard, swerve and stay alert, not just the number of weeks. Clearance comes from your treating doctor.\n\nWhat can help: try a parked-car test with firm brake stamps and quick steering turns, pain-free; know that a left-leg injury in an automatic may be ready earlier than the right leg; don't drive in a sling or a boot on the driving leg without medical advice; keep first drives short, local and off-peak.\n\nHold off if you hesitate on an emergency stop, can't steer with both hands, or anything affects alertness.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
